<% content_for(:title, "Portfolio · McRitchie Studio") %>
<% content_for(:full_width, true) %>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center section-padding">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-heading tracking-tight">Portfolio</h1>
  <p class="text-secondary text-lg mt-4 leading-relaxed">Real apps, live today. Open one and look around.</p>
</section>

<%# The apps ride the engine's carousel (studio/_carousel), the apps' standard for a
    set too long to grid, in its cascade style (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-08): a looping
    3D stack, the open app in front and two each side stepping back (three on a phone).
    portfolio_carousel_style picks it once the installed engine has it (task
    carousel-cascade-style) and keeps the spotlight on an engine before it.
    Each slide is the app's still and nothing else; the name, host and blurb are
    the caption (websites/_portfolio_caption), which both styles show under the
    open slide only, so it changes as the row moves (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-08).
    The card is websites/_portfolio_card; /build keeps its own gallery card. The open
    app's card wears a violet ring (portfolio-row, app/assets/tailwind/build_cards.css).
    Autoplay and loop (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-06) are the engine's: the row asks for
    them through carousel_optional_locals, which passes only the locals the installed
    studio/_carousel declares, so the page autoplays once the engine that has them
    (task carousel-autoplay-and-loop) is installed. %>
<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
  <%= render layout: "studio/carousel",
        locals: { label: "Live apps", items: @examples, per_view: 3, id: "websites-apps", style: portfolio_carousel_style, class_name: "portfolio-row",
                  slide_label: ->(example) { example.name },
                  caption: ->(example) { render("websites/portfolio_caption", example: example) }, data: { test: "websites-carousel" } }
                  .merge(carousel_optional_locals(autoplay: 6, loop: true)) do |example| %>
    <%= render "websites/portfolio_card", example: example %>
  <% end %>
  <%# Under the row and its controls, centred (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-08). %>
  <div class="mt-8 text-center">
    <%= link_to "Build yours", build_path, class: "btn btn-primary", data: { test: "websites-build-cta" } %>
  </div>
</div>
